const ECONOMICS = [{"id":"needs-1","section":"needs","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"A need is something a living thing must have to be able to live.","more":""},{"id":"needs-2","section":"needs","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"Humans have bodily needs of water, food, clothing and shelter to live.","more":""},{"id":"needs-3","section":"needs","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"The need for water is the most important, because a person will die very quickly without drinking water.","more":""},{"id":"needs-4","section":"needs","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"A want is a wish or a desire for something. A person could choose not to have a want.","more":""},{"id":"needs-5","section":"needs","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"A person can need to eat food and can want to eat cake. If there is no cake, the person may eat bread.","more":""},{"id":"needs-6","section":"needs","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"Economics is the study of how people make choices to get what they want.","more":""},{"id":"choices-1","section":"choices","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"Scarcity is when there is not a lot of something.","more":""},{"id":"choices-2","section":"choices","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"Scarcity happens because people always want something new, but resources are limited.","more":""},{"id":"choices-3","section":"choices","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"Scarcity is called the basic problem of economics. It never goes away.","more":""},{"id":"choices-4","section":"choices","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"Scarce things have higher prices. Gold costs much more than iron, because gold is more scarce.","more":""},{"id":"choices-5","section":"choices","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"Opportunity cost is the value of the next best thing you give up whenever you make a decision.","more":""},{"id":"choices-6","section":"choices","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"Going to work means more income but less free time. Staying at home means more free time but less income.","more":""},{"id":"goods-1","section":"goods","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"A good is a physical thing that can be handed to a buyer. A service is not a thing, but an action that helps someone.","more":""},{"id":"goods-2","section":"goods","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"A bicycle is a good. The work of a doctor is a service.","more":""},{"id":"goods-3","section":"goods","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"People who make things are called producers. People who buy things are called consumers. Everyone buys things, so everyone is a consumer.","more":""},{"id":"goods-4","section":"goods","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"Without people who want to buy, producers have no reason to make things. A producer makes things mainly to sell them to consumers.","more":""},{"id":"goods-5","section":"goods","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"Making things takes four kinds of help: labor (work), land, capital (machines and buildings) and enterprise (people who make the decisions).","more":""},{"id":"goods-6","section":"goods","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"Capital goods are goods that are needed to produce other goods. Buildings, equipment and machines are examples.","more":""},{"id":"money-1","section":"money","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"Money is anything that people use to buy goods and services.","more":""},{"id":"money-2","section":"money","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"Barter means trading things directly, without using money. Bob needs shoes and John has shoes, but Bob has eggs and John needs milk. Money fixes that, because anything can be traded for a set amount of money.","more":""},{"id":"money-3","section":"money","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"Money is easier to divide than cows. A person who wants only half a cow's worth of wheat does not want to cut a cow in half.","more":""},{"id":"money-4","section":"money","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"Cows die and wheat rots, but money lasts longer than most trade goods.","more":""},{"id":"money-5","section":"money","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"The first metal coins were made in a country called Lydia, in the western part of what is now Turkey. They were stamped with a picture of a lion.","more":""},{"id":"money-6","section":"money","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"Carrying a lot of silver or gold was hard and dangerous, so banknotes were made. A banknote was a promise to give an amount of precious metal to anyone who brought the paper.","more":""},{"id":"trade-1","section":"trade","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"To trade is to willingly give things or services and get other things or services in return.","more":""},{"id":"trade-2","section":"trade","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"A place where trading takes place is called a market.","more":""},{"id":"trade-3","section":"trade","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"When money is part of a trade, the person who gives the money is buying, and the person who gets the money is selling.","more":""},{"id":"trade-4","section":"trade","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"International trade is trade between countries. A business in one country can sell goods to other countries (exports) or buy goods from them (imports).","more":""},{"id":"trade-5","section":"trade","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"Governments sometimes take some of the money or goods in a trade between countries. This is a kind of tax called a tariff.","more":""},{"id":"trade-6","section":"trade","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"A shipping container is a large steel box. It can go from a ship to a train to a truck without anyone unloading and reloading the cargo.","more":""},{"id":"work-1","section":"work","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"A job is work that a person does to earn money.","more":""},{"id":"work-2","section":"work","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"A teacher's job is to teach. A taxi driver's job is to drive people. A firefighter rescues people from burning buildings and puts out fires.","more":""},{"id":"work-3","section":"work","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"A wage is money that is paid by an employer to an employee in exchange for work.","more":""},{"id":"work-4","section":"work","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"Wages are usually paid by the hour, which is called an hourly wage. In many countries, laws set a minimum wage that all employers must pay their workers.","more":""},{"id":"work-5","section":"work","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"In large cities, one man may earn a living just by mending shoes. A person who does only one very specialised task will do it best.","more":""},{"id":"work-6","section":"work","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"Ten workers who each did one small step of making pins could make upwards of forty-eight thousand pins in a day. Working separately, each could not make twenty pins in a day, perhaps not even one.","more":""},{"id":"business-1","section":"business","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"A business is a place where people work together to make and sell products or services.","more":""},{"id":"business-2","section":"business","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"An entrepreneur is a person who starts a business instead of working for someone else.","more":""},{"id":"business-3","section":"business","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"Many new businesses fail, lose money, and close. An entrepreneur takes on the risks and the rewards of a business.","more":""},{"id":"business-4","section":"business","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"Profit is found by subtracting how much money was spent from how much money was brought in.","more":""},{"id":"business-5","section":"business","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"If John spends $15 on ice cream cones and sells them for $20, he has made a profit of $5.","more":""},{"id":"business-6","section":"business","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"A business can be small or big. One person can open a small barber-shop, and a big business can employ thousands of people all over the world.","more":""},{"id":"supply-1","section":"supply","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"Price is the value of a product or service. A price can be expressed in other goods, in services, or in money.","more":""},{"id":"supply-2","section":"supply","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"Peter will not trade his wool for eggs if he does not need eggs. So Sally sells her eggs for money and gives Peter money for the wool. How much money Peter wants for his wool is the price.","more":""},{"id":"supply-3","section":"supply","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"Two things make a price go up or down. One is the number of things people can buy (supply). The other is the number of things people want to buy (demand).","more":""},{"id":"supply-4","section":"supply","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"If more people want to buy something but the supply stays the same, there will be a shortage, and the price will go up.","more":""},{"id":"supply-5","section":"supply","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"If the supply goes up and the demand stays the same, there will be a surplus, and the price will go down.","more":""},{"id":"supply-6","section":"supply","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"Inflation means that prices are going up. More money is needed to pay for goods, like a loaf of bread.","more":""},{"id":"saving-1","section":"saving","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"Saving is money that is not spent. One way to save is to put money in a savings account.","more":""},{"id":"saving-2","section":"saving","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"A bank is a place where customers can save or borrow money. Customers can put their money in the bank for safekeeping.","more":""},{"id":"saving-3","section":"saving","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"Interest is the cost for borrowing money or the payment for lending money. It is usually a percentage of the money borrowed.","more":""},{"id":"saving-4","section":"saving","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"If the interest on $100 is 1 percent per year, then every year the borrower must pay $1.","more":""},{"id":"saving-5","section":"saving","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"A budget is a plan for the money a person or group will spend. It lists what to spend money on and how much to spend on each.","more":""},{"id":"saving-6","section":"saving","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"A loan is a type of debt. The borrower agrees to pay the lender back at a particular time.","more":""},{"id":"taxes-1","section":"taxes","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"Tax is money that people have to pay to the government.","more":""},{"id":"taxes-2","section":"taxes","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"Taxes pay for people who work for the government, such as the military and police. They also pay for services such as education and health care, and for roads, bridges and sewers.","more":""},{"id":"taxes-3","section":"taxes","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"A sales tax is based on how much a person buys. An income tax is based on how much a person earns. A property tax is based on how much a person owns.","more":""},{"id":"taxes-4","section":"taxes","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"The earliest known taxes were those of the Egyptian Old Kingdom.","more":""},{"id":"taxes-5","section":"taxes","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"Governments use some tax money to pay for public goods, like street lights, that are available for everyone.","more":""},{"id":"taxes-6","section":"taxes","cat":"howworks","kind":"record","text":"In the United States, the national government has an income tax. Most states have an income tax or a sales tax, or both. Cities and towns may have a sales tax or a property tax.","more":""}];
